<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>🌊 LIVE WAVE HEIGHT</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/wave_height/legend.png?v=glwu-20261008-1300Z" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Wave height (feet, 18 fixed colors): <b>0 ft</b> → <b>0.5 ft</b> → <b>1-2 ft</b> → <b>3-4 ft</b> → <b>4-5 ft</b> → <b>6-7 ft</b> → <b>8-9 ft</b> → <b>10-11 ft</b> → <b>12-13 ft</b> → <b>14-15 ft</b> → <b>16-17 ft</b> → <b>18-19 ft</b> → <b>20-21 ft</b> → <b>22-23 ft</b> → <b>24-25 ft</b> → <b>26-27 ft</b> → <b>28-29 ft</b> → <b>30+ ft</b> (white). Every pixel shows its bin's exact color; the legend is the full table. Model maximum this run: <b>7.8 ft</b>. Values above 30 ft stay white. Significant height = average of highest third of waves.</p><p><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT MODEL (analysis)</p><p><b>Source:</b> NOAA/NCEP Great Lakes Wave Unstructured v2.1 (GLWUv2.1, WAVEWATCH III)<br/><a href="https://nomads.ncep.noaa.gov/pub/data/nccf/com/glwu/prod/glwu.20261008/glwu.grlc_2p5km.t13z.grib2">https://nomads.ncep.noaa.gov/pub/data/nccf/com/glwu/prod/glwu.20261008/glwu.grlc_2p5km.t13z.grib2</a></p><p>Transparent outside valid water data so existing project layers (shipwrecks, lighthouses, harbors, parks) stay visible. Turn on/off independently of temperature and ice layers.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <GroundOverlay>
      <name>🌊 LIVE WAVE HEIGHT</name>
      <drawOrder>10</drawOrder>
      <Icon>
        <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/wave_height/current.png?v=glwu-20261008-1300Z</href>
        <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
        <refreshInterval>900</refreshInterval>
      </Icon>
      <LatLonBox>
        <north>49.5</north>
        <south>40.5</south>
        <east>-73.5</east>
        <west>-93.0</west>
      </LatLonBox>
    </GroundOverlay>
